{
  "freeTextAnnotations": [
    {
      "id": "b1-title",
      "text": "pruger-20-rtr-all-svc-test",
      "position": {
        "x": 140,
        "y": 100
      },
      "fontSize": 22,
      "fontColor": "#ffffff",
      "backgroundColor": "#0f172a",
      "fontWeight": "bold",
      "roundedBackground": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b1-core-facts",
      "text": "AS 65000  |  IS-IS level 2  |  SR-MPLS, label block 16000 to 23999  |  iBGP to the route reflectors xrv-rtr1 and xrv-rtr2",
      "position": {
        "x": 436,
        "y": 106.5
      },
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontColor": "#94a3b8"
    },
    {
      "id": "b1-services",
      "text": "Services by VLAN:  110 BGP L3VPN  |  210 VPWS, targeted LDP  |  220 VPLS, targeted LDP  |  230 VPWS, EVPN  |  240 EVPN LAN\nEndpoint VLANs:  111 BGP L3VPN  |  220 VPLS  |  240 EVPN LAN  |  21az VPWS, targeted LDP  |  23az VPWS, EVPN   (a = side A kind, z = side B kind: 1 XRv9k, 2 vJunos-router, 3 cJunosEvolved, 4 cEOS)",
      "position": {
        "x": 140,
        "y": 1203.3957900684309
      },
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontColor": "#94a3b8"
    },
    {
      "id": "panel-tests",
      "text": "### Test the services\nOne ping for each service. A reply proves the control plane and the forwarding plane.\nRun on **vjunos-SW1** (the CE of vjunos-RTR1), if no other node is named.\n\n**110  BGP L3VPN**\n- `ping 172.16.0.51 source 172.16.0.41 routing-instance CE`  (replies from srx1)\n- On **xrv-rtr1**: `ping vrf L3VPN-A 172.16.0.41 source 10.100.0.1`\n\n**210  VPWS, targeted LDP**\n- `ping 10.210.0.2 routing-instance CE`  (replies from vjunos-SW3)\n\n**220  VPLS, targeted LDP**\n- `ping 10.220.0.4 routing-instance CE`  (replies from vjunos-SW4)\n\n**230  VPWS, EVPN signaling**\n- `ping 10.230.0.2 routing-instance CE`  (replies from vjunos-SW4)\n\n**240  EVPN LAN**\n- `ping 10.240.0.42 routing-instance CE`  (Junos to Junos, vjunos-SW2)\n- `ping 10.240.0.51 routing-instance CE`  (Junos to cEOS, srx1)",
      "position": {
        "x": 2367.989323843416,
        "y": -226
      },
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontColor": "#e2e8f0",
      "backgroundColor": "#0f172a",
      "width": 640,
      "roundedBackground": true
    },
    {
      "id": "panel-shows",
      "text": "### Show the components\n\n**XRv9k: core and route reflector**\n- `show isis adjacency`\n- `show isis segment-routing label table`\n- `show bgp vpnv4 unicast summary`\n- `show bgp l2vpn evpn summary`\n- `show cef 10.255.0.11/32`\n\n**vJunos-router: PE for all services**\n- `show isis adjacency`\n- `show isis overview | match SRGB`\n- `show route table inet.3`\n- `show bgp summary`\n- `show l2circuit connections`\n- `show vpls connections`\n- `show evpn vpws-instance`\n- `show evpn database instance EVPN-240`\n\n**cJunosEvolved: L3VPN PE**\n- `show isis adjacency`\n- `show bgp summary`\n- `show route table L3VPN-A.inet.0`\n\n**cEOS: L3VPN and EVPN LAN PE**\n- `show isis segment-routing tunnel`\n- `show bgp evpn summary`\n- `show bgp evpn route-type imet`\n- `show mac address-table vlan 240`\n- `show mpls label ranges`\n\n**CE: vSRX and vJunos-switch**\n- `show bgp summary`\n- `show route 172.16.0.41`\n- `show arp no-resolve`\n\n**Packet capture on cEOS, core port**\n- `bash sudo tcpdump -ne -XX -i eth2 -c 3 mpls`",
      "position": {
        "x": 2434.154615026948,
        "y": 664
      },
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontColor": "#e2e8f0",
      "backgroundColor": "#0f172a",
      "width": 640,
      "roundedBackground": true
    },
    {
      "id": "panel-endpoints",
      "text": "### Test the endpoints (vSRX)\nState: written from the vendor syntax, not tested. The node `validator` runs all of these checks: `bash /opt/validator/validate.sh` (docs/LAB-VALIDATOR.md). Full list: `labs/pruger-20-rtr-all-svc-test-configs/VERIFY.md`, section 5.\nPing script for each endpoint: `labs/pruger-20-rtr-all-svc-test-configs/checks/ep-NODE.txt`.\n\n**Side A (right):** xrv-rtr2, vjunos-RTR2, evo-rtr2, CEOS2.  **Side B (left):** xrv-rtr3, vjunos-RTR3, evo-rtr3, CEOS3.\n**LAN endpoints** (111, 220, 240): srx13, srx22, srx20, srx19, srx8, srx7, srx5, srx4.\n**VPWS endpoints** (21az, 23az): srx23, srx17, srx15, srx14, srx18, srx12, srx10, srx9.\n\n**LAN endpoint, run on srx22** (CE of vjunos-RTR2)\n- `ping 172.16.0.107 source 172.16.0.122`  (111 L3VPN, to srx7 on vjunos-RTR3)\n- `ping 172.16.0.113 source 172.16.0.122`  (111 L3VPN, to srx13 on xrv-rtr2)\n- `ping 10.220.0.120`  (220 VPLS, to srx20 on evo-rtr2)\n- `ping 10.220.0.119`  (220 VPLS, to srx19 on CEOS2)\n- `ping 10.240.0.105`  (240 EVPN LAN, to srx5 on evo-rtr3)\n- `ping 10.240.0.104`  (240 EVPN LAN, to srx4 on CEOS3)\n\n**VPWS endpoint, run on srx17** (CE of vjunos-RTR2, side A, kind 2)\n- `ping 10.21.21.2`  (2121, targeted LDP, to XRv9k)\n- `ping 10.21.22.2`  (2122, targeted LDP, to vJunos-router)\n- `ping 10.21.23.2`  (2123, targeted LDP, to cJunosEvolved)\n- `ping 10.21.24.2`  (2124, targeted LDP, to cEOS)\n- `ping 10.23.21.2`  (2321, EVPN, to XRv9k)\n- `ping 10.23.22.2`  (2322, EVPN, to vJunos-router)\n- `ping 10.23.23.2`  (2323, EVPN, to cJunosEvolved)\n- `ping 10.23.24.2`  (2324, EVPN, to cEOS)\n\n**State on the PE**\n- `show l2circuit connections`  (Junos)\n- `show evpn vpws-instance`  (Junos)\n- `show vpls connections`  (Junos)\n- `show l2vpn xconnect`  (XRv9k)\n- `show patch panel`  (cEOS)\n- `show vpls`  (cEOS)",
      "position": {
        "x": 3057.989323843416,
        "y": -226
      },
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontColor": "#e2e8f0",
      "backgroundColor": "#0f172a",
      "width": 640,
      "roundedBackground": true
    }
